  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1202.14 Cooling water",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1202.14 “Cooling water” means the clean wastewater from air conditioning, industrial cooling, condensing, and similar apparatus and from hydraulically-powered equipment that is sufficiently clean, uncontaminated, and unpolluted that it can be discharged, without treatment or purification, to a natural open stream or watercourse, subject to the conditions of an NPDES permit.\n\nSource. #8235, eff 12-22-04 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1200) (formerly Env-Ws 1202.14); ss by #9798, ef 10-9-10 (from Env-Wq 1202.13); ss by #12739, eff 3-19-19",
